---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Rules & Contest Integrity // DHPMCC">
  <section id="rules" class="content-container rules-section">
    <header class="rules-header">
      <h1 class="page-title">Rules &amp; Contest Integrity</h1>
      <p class="page-subtitle"><em>Essential guidelines governing eligibility, fair play, submissions, and automated scoring.</em></p>
    </header>

    <div class="rules-preamble">
      <p>
        DHPMCC is conducted under strict competitive programming regulations. Competitors are expected to read and adhere to all contest conduct guidelines before beginning the competition.
      </p>
    </div>

    <nav class="rules-toc" aria-label="Table of Contents">
      <span class="toc-label">Jump to section:</span>
      <ul class="toc-list">
        <li><a href="#eligibility">Eligibility &amp; Participation</a></li>
        <li><a href="#timing">Contest Timing</a></li>
        <li><a href="#assistance">Allowed Assistance &amp; Resources</a></li>
        <li><a href="#languages">Supported Languages &amp; Tools</a></li>
        <li><a href="#io">Input &amp; Output</a></li>
        <li><a href="#judging">Submissions &amp; Judging</a></li>
        <li><a href="#integrity">Contest Integrity &amp; Security</a></li>
        <li><a href="#problems">Problem Integrity</a></li>
        <li><a href="#disqualification">Disqualification</a></li>
      </ul>
    </nav>

    <div class="rules-body">
      <section id="eligibility" class="rule-block">
        <h2 class="rule-section-title">Eligibility &amp; Participation</h2>
        <ul class="rule-list">
          <li><strong>Individual Competition:</strong> DHPMCC is an individual competition. Each competitor must work independently and may not receive assistance from another competitor, coach, teacher, parent, or other person during the contest.</li>
          <li><strong>One Contestant, One Account:</strong> Each competitor may participate using only their own registered contest account. Sharing accounts or credentials is prohibited.</li>
          <li><strong>Contest Registration:</strong> Competitors must register before the stated registration deadline and provide accurate information.</li>
          <li><strong>Division Eligibility:</strong> Competitors must compete in the division corresponding to their grade level as defined by the official DHPMCC rules. Competitors may not intentionally enter a different division to gain a competitive advantage.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="timing" class="rule-block">
        <h2 class="rule-section-title">Contest Timing</h2>
        <ul class="rule-list">
          <li><strong>Contest Window:</strong> The competition runs within a strictly monitored, synchronized time window.</li>
          <li><strong>Official Clock:</strong> The live contest clock displayed on the contest platform is the authoritative source for the contest start and end times.</li>
          <li><strong>Late Submissions:</strong> No submissions will be accepted after the contest termination signal.</li>
          <li><strong>Early Start:</strong> Competitors may not access contest problems or begin working before the official start time.</li>
          <li><strong>Breaks:</strong> Competitors may take breaks as permitted by the contest environment, but the contest clock will continue running.</li>
          <li><strong>Technical Issues:</strong> Competitors should report technical problems to contest staff as soon as they occur. Technical difficulties do not automatically extend the contest window.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="assistance" class="rule-block">
        <h2 class="rule-section-title">Allowed Assistance &amp; Resources</h2>
        <ul class="rule-list">
          <li><strong>Independent Work:</strong> All submitted solutions must be conceived and written entirely by the competitor during the contest window.</li>
          <li><strong>Prohibited Collaboration:</strong> Discussing problems, algorithms, test cases, code, or solutions with other people during the contest is prohibited.</li>
          <li><strong>External Assistance:</strong> Competitors may not use another person or an external service to solve, debug, optimize, or generate contest solutions.</li>
          <li><strong>AI &amp; Code Generation:</strong> AI assistants, code-generation tools, and automated problem-solving systems are prohibited unless the contest organizers explicitly announce otherwise.</li>
          <li><strong>Solution Sharing:</strong> Competitors may not publish, transmit, or otherwise share contest problems, solutions, or substantial portions of their work with other competitors during the contest.</li>
          <li><strong>Permitted References:</strong> Officially permitted documentation and language references may be used if explicitly allowed by the contest organizers. Contest-specific restrictions take precedence over general platform capabilities.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="languages" class="rule-block">
        <h2 class="rule-section-title">Supported Languages &amp; Tools</h2>
        <ul class="rule-list">
          <li><strong>Supported Languages:</strong> Participants may submit solutions in C, C++17, Java, or Python 3.12.</li>
          <li><strong>Standard Libraries:</strong> Solutions may use the standard libraries provided by their selected language.</li>
          <li><strong>Third-Party Packages:</strong> Third-party packages and libraries are not permitted unless explicitly provided or authorized by the contest organizers.</li>
          <li><strong>Network Access:</strong> Contest programs may not make external network requests. Network access is blocked within the judging environment.</li>
          <li><strong>Compiler &amp; Runtime:</strong> Submissions are compiled and executed using the contest platform’s official judging environment. Competitors should not rely on compiler-specific behavior outside the stated language specifications.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="io" class="rule-block">
        <h2 class="rule-section-title">Input &amp; Output</h2>
        <ul class="rule-list">
          <li><strong>Standard Input:</strong> Problems read input from standard input (stdin).</li>
          <li><strong>Standard Output:</strong> Solutions must write their answers to standard output (stdout).</li>
          <li><strong>No File I/O:</strong> Reading from or writing to files is prohibited unless a problem explicitly states otherwise.</li>
          <li><strong>Output Format:</strong> Output must follow the exact format specified in the problem statement.</li>
          <li><strong>Debug Output:</strong> Additional output, including debugging messages, may cause a submission to receive a Wrong Answer verdict.</li>
          <li><strong>Whitespace:</strong> Unless the problem statement specifies otherwise, output should contain only the requested information.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="judging" class="rule-block">
        <h2 class="rule-section-title">Submissions &amp; Judging</h2>
        <ul class="rule-list">
          <li><strong>Automated Judging:</strong> Every submission is evaluated automatically against the official test suite.</li>
          <li><strong>Submission Limits:</strong> If a problem has a submission limit, exceeding that limit is prohibited and additional submissions will not be accepted.</li>
          <li><strong>Independent Evaluation:</strong> Each submission is judged independently. A previous submission’s verdict does not guarantee anything about subsequent submissions.</li>
          <li>
            <strong>Verdicts:</strong> Possible verdicts include:
            <ul class="verdicts-sublist">
              <li><strong>Accepted (AC):</strong> The solution passed all required tests.</li>
              <li><strong>Wrong Answer (WA):</strong> The output was incorrect for one or more tests.</li>
              <li><strong>Time Limit Exceeded (TLE):</strong> The program exceeded the permitted execution time.</li>
              <li><strong>Memory Limit Exceeded (MLE):</strong> The program exceeded the permitted memory limit.</li>
              <li><strong>Runtime Error (RTE):</strong> The program terminated unexpectedly during execution.</li>
              <li><strong>Compilation Error (CE):</strong> The submission could not be compiled successfully.</li>
            </ul>
          </li>
          <li><strong>Hidden Tests:</strong> Competitors should assume that official tests may include cases not shown in the sample input.</li>
          <li><strong>Judge Data:</strong> Official test data, expected outputs, and judging infrastructure are not available to competitors.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="integrity" class="rule-block">
        <h2 class="rule-section-title">Contest Integrity &amp; Security</h2>
        <ul class="rule-list">
          <li><strong>Academic Integrity:</strong> Competitors are expected to uphold the standards of academic integrity established by Bergen County Academies.</li>
          <li><strong>No Screen Sharing or Observation:</strong> Competitors may not view another competitor’s screen, code, submissions, or contest activity.</li>
          <li><strong>No Unauthorized Devices:</strong> Competitors may not use additional computers, phones, tablets, or other devices for prohibited assistance.</li>
          <li><strong>Judge Manipulation:</strong> Attempting to exploit, modify, interfere with, or tamper with the judging system or contest infrastructure is strictly prohibited.</li>
          <li><strong>Platform Exploitation:</strong> Deliberately exploiting vulnerabilities in the contest platform, judge, or infrastructure to obtain an unfair advantage is prohibited.</li>
          <li><strong>Credential Security:</strong> Competitors are responsible for keeping their contest credentials private.</li>
          <li><strong>Impersonation:</strong> Submitting work under another competitor’s account or allowing another person to submit on one’s behalf is prohibited.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="problems" class="rule-block">
        <h2 class="rule-section-title">Problem Integrity</h2>
        <ul class="rule-list">
          <li><strong>Confidentiality:</strong> Contest problems and materials must not be shared with competitors who have not yet begun or completed the contest, as applicable.</li>
          <li><strong>No Early Access:</strong> Accessing leaked, improperly distributed, or otherwise unauthorized contest materials before the official contest time is prohibited.</li>
          <li><strong>Problem Clarifications:</strong> Questions about a problem’s interpretation should be directed only through the official contest communication channel.</li>
          <li><strong>Official Clarifications:</strong> If organizers issue a clarification or correction, it applies to all competitors and supersedes conflicting information in the original statement.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="disqualification" class="rule-block disqualification-block">
        <h2 class="rule-section-title">Disqualification</h2>
        <p class="disqualification-intro">A competitor may be disqualified for:</p>
        <ul class="rule-list disqualification-list">
          <li>Unauthorized collaboration or assistance.</li>
          <li>Use of prohibited external resources or AI tools.</li>
          <li>Sharing solutions or contest materials during the contest.</li>
          <li>Using another competitor’s account.</li>
          <li>Tampering with judging or contest infrastructure.</li>
          <li>Attempting to obtain unauthorized access to contest data.</li>
          <li>Deliberately disrupting the contest for other competitors.</li>
          <li>Any other conduct determined by contest officials to provide an unfair competitive advantage.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="disqualification-notice">
          <p>Contest officials reserve the right to investigate suspicious submissions or activity and make final determinations regarding rule violations and disqualification.</p>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .rules-section {
    padding-top: 2rem;
  }

  .rules-header {
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .page-title {
    font-size: 1.9rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: #111111;
    margin: 0 0 0.4rem 0;
  }

  .page-subtitle {
    color: #555555;
    font-size: 1rem;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .rules-preamble {
    font-size: 1.02rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: #2d3748;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .rules-preamble p {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .rules-toc {
    background-color: var(--color-bg-subtle);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    padding: 0.85rem 1.15rem;
    border-radius: 4px;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
    font-size: 0.92rem;
  }

  .toc-label {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: #111111;
    display: inline-block;
    margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
  }

  .toc-list {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.4rem 1.25rem;
    list-style: none;
    padding-left: 0;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .toc-list li {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .toc-list a {
    color: var(--color-link);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .toc-list a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
    color: var(--color-link-hover);
  }

  .rules-body {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 2.25rem;
  }

  .rule-block {
    scroll-margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }

  .rule-section-title {
    font-size: 1.28rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: #111111;
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem 0;
    padding-bottom: 0.35rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .rule-list {
    list-style-type: disc;
    padding-left: 1.4rem;
    margin: 0.5rem 0 0 0;
  }

  .rule-list > li {
    font-size: 0.98rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: #2d3748;
    margin-bottom: 0.65rem;
  }

  .rule-list > li strong {
    color: #111111;
  }

  .verdicts-sublist {
    list-style-type: circle;
    padding-left: 1.4rem;
    margin: 0.4rem 0 0.2rem 0;
  }

  .verdicts-sublist li {
    margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  .disqualification-intro {
    font-size: 0.98rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: #2d3748;
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem 0;
  }

  .disqualification-list {
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }

  .disqualification-notice {
    background-color: #fdf8f8;
    border-left: 3px solid #8b0000;
    padding: 0.85rem 1.15rem;
    border-radius: 0 4px 4px 0;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: #2d3748;
  }

  .disqualification-notice p {
    margin: 0;
    font-style: italic;
  }

  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .toc-list {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 0.3rem;
    }
  }
</style>
